'' RUN: OVERLOAD JOINS A NAME WHOSE FIRST DECLARATION DID NOT WRITE IT -- tiko's divergence
'' (RFC-0001 F4): a later 'declare ... overload', a definition after a plain or an ALIAS
'' declare, one after a body written without the keyword (which must mangle as an overload
'' too), and overloads of windows.bi's GetWindowText and GetWindowRect, one of them with
'' the API's own arity. Each call picks by signature; Windows' own still answer theirs.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/codegen/src/overload-join.tiko -o tests/codegen/overload-join.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/overload-join.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  42 F:x 3.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2 P:a 3 Q:b 4 R:c
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: t0 0 5 into
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -7 0
